Notes on this run
 - "needs manual review: [color-contrast]" on the pages with a card: axe cannot measure the three arrow glyphs (left, right, up) that are
   drawn inside the keyboard hints ("Element content contains only non-text characters"). They inherit the colour of their button, so the
   ratio is the one of the label next to them, which axe did measure and pass: 7.83:1 (ink on accent, Like button) and 16.55:1 (text on
   surface, the other buttons), computed from the design tokens.
 - The single console line "Failed to load resource ... 500" is the one that this script causes on purpose in section 9, by answering
   /api/profiles with a 500 to show the error state. There was no other console message, warning or page error.
 - Section 5 uses Chrome's touch emulation through the DevTools protocol (Input.dispatchTouchEvent), not a physical phone.
